<title>INDIA: India's CARE sets ratings for debt instruments.</title>
<headline>India's CARE sets ratings for debt instruments.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Credit Analysis &amp; Research Ltd (CARE) has announced ratings for debt issues of the following companies.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p> Company		 Instrument  Rating   Issue size(Rupees)/</p>
<p>							    Comments</p>
<p>* KGK Finance Ltd.	   FD    CARE BBB(FD)  (Upto 20 million)</p>
<p>					    Rating	  Size enhanced</p>
<p>					    reaffirmed   from 15 million</p>
<p>* Ram Kaashyap Investments FD    CARE BBB+(FD) (Upto 220 million)</p>
<p>					    Rating</p>
<p>					    reaffirmed</p>
<p>* Sanmac Motor Finance     FD    CARE A+(FD)   (Upto 400 million)</p>
<p>					    Rating	  Size enhanced</p>
<p>					    reaffirmed   from 375 million</p>
<p>* Thirunindra Narayanan</p>
<p>  Finance &amp; Investment (P) FD    CARE BBB(FD)  (Upto 50 million)</p>
<p>					    Rating	  Size enhanced</p>
<p>					    reaffirmed   from 40 million</p>
<p>* Suraj Securities &amp; Fin.  FD    CARE C(FD)    (Upto 50 million)</p>
<p>					    Downgraded</p>
<p>					    from</p>
<p>					    CARE BBB(FD)</p>
<p>* DCM Financial Services   FD    CARE A(FD)    (Upto 1000 million)</p>
<p>					    Downgraded</p>
<p>					    from</p>
<p>					    CARE AA-(FD)</p>
<p>				 NCD(A)  CARE A(SO)    (200 million)</p>
<p>					    Downgraded</p>
<p>					    from</p>
<p>					    CARE AA-(SO)</p>
<p>				 NCD(B)  CARE A	  (300 million)</p>
<p>					    Downgraded</p>
<p>					    from</p>
<p>					    CARE A+</p>
<p>* Srei International</p>
<p>  Finance			FD    CARE AA-(FD)  (Upto 400 million)</p>
<p>					    Downgraded    Size enhanced</p>
<p>					    from	    from 300 million</p>
<p>					    CARE AA(FD)</p>
<p>				 Bonds   CARE A+	 (42.7 million)</p>
<p>					    Downgraded</p>
<p>					    from</p>
<p>					    CARE AA-</p>
<p>				 NCD     CARE A+	 (200 million)</p>
<p>					    Downgraded</p>
<p>					    from</p>
<p>					    CARE AA-</p>
<p>* Olympia Capitals	  FD     CARE C(FD)    (25 million)</p>
<p>					    Downgraded</p>
<p>					    from</p>
<p>					    CARE BBB+(FD)</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>    FRB    -  Floating rate bonds</p>
<p>    CP     -  Commercial paper</p>
<p>    CD     -  Certificate of Deposit</p>
<p>    PCD    -  Partly convertible debenture</p>
<p>    FD     -  Fixed Deposit</p>
<p>    OCD    -  Optionally convertible debenture</p>
<p>    NCD    -  Non-convertible debenture</p>
<p>    PCN    -  Partly convertible notes.</p>
<p>    ICD    -  Inter Corporate Deposit</p>
<p>    CCPS   -  Cumulative convertible preference shares</p>
<p>    OFCD   -  Optionally fully convertible debentures.</p>
<p>    DDB    -  Deep Discount Bond</p>
<p>    CAR    -  Credit Analysis Rating</p>
<p>    SO     -  Structural Obligation</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>Note : PR1 is a symbol for superior, PR2 for strong, PR3 adequate, PR4 risk prone and PR5 default. The plus or minus sign after the rating indicates the relative position within the band covered by the symbol.</p>
<p>CARE AA(FD) indicates high quality, CARE A(FD) indicates adequate safety, CARE BBB(FD) indicates moderate safety, CARE AAA(FD) indicates best quality, CARE BB(FD) indicates inadequate safety, CARE B(FD) indicates risk prone, CARE C(FD) indicates high risk, and CARE D(FD) indicates default.</p>
